
 Move decsdata datasets into a dated cold storage directory and hand them to the
 GLADE HSM to be migrated onto tape.  Each dataset directory is moved from the
 decsdata directory into '<decsdata>/cold_storage_<date>/' and then passed to
 'glade_hsm migrate', which relocates it once more into a 'COLD_STORAGE/'
 sub-directory, ending up as:

    <decsdata>/cold_storage_<date>/COLD_STORAGE/<dsid>

 The HSM batch processes then migrate every large file (>= 100MB) underneath the
 'COLD_STORAGE/' path onto tape.  All files inside a 'COLD_STORAGE/' path are
 marked immutable, which prevents modification of their contents and metadata.
 Use 'decsdata_restore' to bring the data back.

 Usage: decsdata_storage [-D Date] [-w DecsdataDirectory] [-l ListFile]  \
                         [-d DatasetList] -x

      - Option -D Date, the cold storage date, in YYYYMMDD or YYYY-MM-DD.  It
          names the cold storage directory '<decsdata>/cold_storage_<date>'.
          Defaults to today;

      - Option -w DecsdataDirectory, the decsdata directory the datasets are
          stored from, and the directory the cold storage directory is created
          in.  Defaults to the configured decsdata root path, /gdex/decsdata;

      - Option -l ListFile, a file holding one dataset ID per line.  Only used
          if -d is not given.  Defaults to 'dsids_<date>.lst' in the current
          directory, which is generated from every dNNNNNN directory found in
          the decsdata directory if it does not exist yet;

      - Option -d DatasetList, one or more dataset IDs to move into cold
          storage, such as '-d d612000 d627000';

      - Option -h, display this help document;

      - Option -x, execute the cold storage moves.  This option is mandatory;
          this help document is displayed without it.  Note that no
          confirmation is asked for once -x is given.

  This utility can be run from any directory.  It is executed under the
  effective user 'gdexdata' via setuid, so the moved data keeps its ownership.
  A dataset is skipped, and an error is logged, if it is not an existing
  directory in the decsdata directory or if it cannot be moved.

  Examples:

    1. Move two given datasets into today's cold storage:

          decsdata_storage -d d612000 d627000 -x

    2. Move them into the cold storage directory of a specific date:

          decsdata_storage -D 20250529 -d d612000 -x

       The data then ends up in:

          /gdex/decsdata/cold_storage_20250529/COLD_STORAGE/d612000

    3. Move every dataset listed in a list file:

          decsdata_storage -l my_dsids.lst -x

    4. Move every dNNNNNN dataset found in a non-default decsdata directory,
       generating the dataset list file automatically:

          decsdata_storage -w /PathTo/decsdata -x
